    "Let R=2^64, M=product(p_i), B_i=M/p_i, gamma_i=(residue_i*inverse(B_i mod p_i)) mod p_i. The centered representative is sum(gamma_i*B_i)-round(sum(gamma_i/p_i))*M.",
    "With rho_i=floor(R/p_i), S=sum(gamma_i*rho_i), E=sum(gamma_i), we have S<=R*sum(gamma_i/p_i)<=S+E. Products gamma_i*rho_i<R; S<17R and E<17*2^30, so uint64 products and uint128 sums cannot overflow.",
    "The two integer quotients floor((S+R/2)/R) and floor((S+E+R/2)/R) enclose the exact rounded quotient. If equal, reconstruct directly modulo the requested output width; otherwise call original Garner CRT on the original residues.",
    "Canonical residues, immutable precomputed CRT bases and integer reciprocals, block-local workspace, and exact boundary fallback preserve thread safety and arbitrary output torus widths."
